pwm: imx27: support the Glowforge fsl,extra-prescale divider

ForgeFIRM laser-power fix. The factory 4.14 tree carried
fsl,extra-prescale = <13> on the laser PWM (via its 1001 patch): the
glowforge.ko cnc engine programs a ~1925 ns period so the SDMA script
can write raw 7-bit power levels straight into PWMSAR, and the extra
prescaler stretches the actual output to ~25 us / ~40 kHz - the
carrier the laser PSU expects - without changing the valid duty range.
The 6.12 port dropped this (wrongly triaged as audio-only), leaving
the laser PWM at ~520 kHz. There is no DT-only workaround: requesting
25 us directly gives PWMPR ~1650 and caps the script's 7-bit writes at
~8% duty.

Re-derive against mainline pwm-imx27: multiply only the PWMCR
prescaler field after the period/duty counts are computed (PWMPR and
the SAR range are unaffected), bounds-check the field, read the
property at probe (default 1 - no behavior change for other users).
get_state() reads the register back and thus reports the stretched
period; consistent, though asymmetric with the requested period, as in
the factory driver.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [embedded specific]
Signed-off-by: Scott Wiederhold <s.e.wiederhold@gmail.com>

--- a/drivers/pwm/pwm-imx27.c
+++ b/drivers/pwm/pwm-imx27.c
@@ -91,6 +91,15 @@ struct pwm_imx27_chip {
 	 * value to return in that case.
 	 */
 	unsigned int duty_cycle;
+
+	/*
+	 * Glowforge (fsl,extra-prescale): additional frequency divider
+	 * applied only to the clock prescaler, stretching the output period
+	 * by this factor without changing the PWMPR count - and therefore
+	 * without changing the range of valid PWMSAR duty values, which the
+	 * Glowforge SDMA script writes directly as raw 7-bit power levels.
+	 */
+	u32 extra_prescale;
 };
 
 static inline struct pwm_imx27_chip *to_pwm_imx27_chip(struct pwm_chip *chip)
@@ -243,6 +252,17 @@ static int pwm_imx27_apply(struct pwm_chip *chip, struct pwm_device *pwm,
 	duty_cycles = c;
 	duty_cycles /= prescale;
 
+	/*
+	 * Glowforge: stretch the output period by the extra prescale factor.
+	 * Applied after the period/duty counts are final so PWMPR and the
+	 * SAR duty range are unaffected; only the prescaler field grows.
+	 * (get_state() reads the register back, so it reports the stretched
+	 * period - consistent, though asymmetric with the requested period.)
+	 */
+	prescale *= imx->extra_prescale;
+	if (prescale > FIELD_MAX(MX3_PWMCR_PRESCALER) + 1)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
 	/*
 	 * according to imx pwm RM, the real period value should be PERIOD
 	 * value in PWMPR plus 2.
@@ -419,6 +439,13 @@ static int pwm_imx27_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		return dev_err_probe(&pdev->dev, PTR_ERR(imx->clk_per),
 				     "failed to get peripheral clock\n");
 
+	/* Glowforge: optional extra output-period divider (default 1). */
+	imx->extra_prescale = 1;
+	of_property_read_u32(pdev->dev.of_node, "fsl,extra-prescale",
+			     &imx->extra_prescale);
+	if (!imx->extra_prescale)
+		imx->extra_prescale = 1;
+
 	chip->ops = &pwm_imx27_ops;
 
 	imx->mmio_base = devm_platform_ioremap_resource(pdev, 0);
